.DS_Store
minecraft-plugin/

# ─── Ansible ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The vault password, never the vault itself. group_vars/production/vault.yml is ENCRYPTED and is
# meant to be committed — that is the point of Ansible Vault. What must never be committed is the
# password that opens it, so the usual in-repo filenames are blocked here as a backstop. The correct
# place for it is outside the checkout entirely: --vault-password-file ~/.robtic-vault
.vault_pass
.vault-pass
*.vault-pass
vault-password
vault_password*
infra/ansible/.vault*

# Rendered artefacts and run state. The production .env is generated on the server and must never
# appear here; the pattern above already covers `.env`, this covers the environment-suffixed forms.
.env.production
.env.staging
infra/ansible/.ansible_facts/
infra/ansible/collections/
*.retry